   $q$Tangent segments $PA$ and $PB$ touch a circle at $A$ and $B$. The circumscribed angle $\angle APB$ measures $(2x + 4)^\circ$ and minor arc $AB$ measures $(3x + 16)^\circ$. What is the measure of $\angle APB$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$20^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-circumscribed-as-inscribed"},{"text":"$68^\\circ$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$32^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-x-instead-of-the-angle"},{"text":"$140^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-360-instead-of-180"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$68^\circ$$q$, $q$A circumscribed angle and the central angle of its minor arc are supplementary, since the two radii meet the tangents at right angles. So $2x + 4 + 3x + 16 = 180$, giving $5x = 160$ and $x = 32$. Then $\angle APB = 2 \cdot 32 + 4 = 68^\circ$. The value $20^\circ$ comes from setting the angle equal to half the arc, which is the rule for inscribed angles.$q$, 'draft', null)
